WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.629
Film Courage: Let’s suppose I’m at a networking
event or I get invited to a great festival

00:00:03.629 --> 00:00:05.460
and it’s a mixer.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:08.549
So someone says “Hey, may I see your work?”

00:00:08.549 --> 00:00:13.089
And I know that it’s probably not ready,
what’s the best way to let them know that

00:00:13.089 --> 00:00:14.169
where I am not hurting their feelings?

00:00:14.169 --> 00:00:16.610
Wendy Kram, owner of Wendy’s LA4hire: Oh,
sure great question.

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:18.010
I would say “That’s fantastic.

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:27.490
I’ doing revisions, can I get your card
and can I send it to you when it’s ready?”

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:32.599
And “Can I drop you an email reminder when
it’s ready?

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:33.599
Sure that would be great.”

00:00:33.599 --> 00:00:39.239
Film Courage: So you are not waiting a year
for the revision you are keeping them in your

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:43.340
mind…er their mind (sorry) “Hi, I met
you and thank you for…”

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:49.030
Wendy: Exactly and you know what, it could
be year if that’s really what it takes?

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:58.820
To me, it’s ready when it’s ready so it
could be “I met you a year ago at Sundance

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:06.540
and I mentioned a sci-fi 1-hour drama that
I have and I finally have it ready and it’s

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:07.540
been vetted.”

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:12.131
And actually I don’t even know if I would
go into all that detail but and here’s a

00:01:12.131 --> 00:01:13.280
brief premise.”

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:14.479
Very, very briefly.

00:01:14.479 --> 00:01:19.600
Executives don’t want a whole big description
because they also can be libel.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:24.840
They don’t want to hear ideas in too much
detail because they are not allowed to accept

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:29.930
them for legal reasons but if it’s someone
that you have met and just to give the a refresher

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:41.360
this is the sci-fi 1-hour pilot about an alien
that comes to earth and can I send it to you?”

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:45.369
And they will either respond and say “Great”
or they might say “No.”

00:01:45.369 --> 00:01:54.159
There also is another subject which is a submission
release forms because a lot of executives

00:01:54.159 --> 00:02:01.530
will not take material without a submission
release form this is if it’s not being submitted

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.579
by an agent or manager.

00:02:03.579 --> 00:02:04.619
Film Courage: Interesting.

00:02:04.619 --> 00:02:09.360
Yeah, I’m wondering if people really understand
that when people…and I’ve seen that on

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:12.380
people’s Twitter bios “I do not take…
[unsolicited material].”

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:13.380
You know?

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:19.090
I see it all the time and for a newbie do
you think they realize the implications of

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:21.640
how it’s a turn off when someone says “No.”

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.330
Like that, they are reasons why.

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:26.820
It’s not because they don’t think your
idea is good, it’s because they are protecting

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:27.820
themselves.

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:37.800
Wendy: Right so then there are ways around
to try and bypass that and yeah that would

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:42.670
probably fall under a whole conversation about
networking and submission policies.

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:46.880
Film Courage: But for someone to respect that
when they see that someone says “We do not

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:48.110
take blind submissions.”

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:49.110
Wendy: Yes.

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:55.250
Well a good counter can be “I’d be happy
to sign a submission release form.”

00:02:55.250 --> 00:03:02.630
And as I say that my disclaimer is that as
I say this I am not an entertainment attorney.

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:03.630
Film Courage: Sure.

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:09.150
Wendy: So whoever may be listening, if you
get a submission release form, I advise you

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:12.450
to show it to an entertainment attorney.

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:21.450
And it is up to you to decide whether to sign
it or not but that is a way around that legality

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:23.860
of them not wanting to accept that at all?

